Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: GRX500: reserve kernel before allocating DT pools

AX50 RAM Ethernet logs place the dynamic jumbo pool at 0x20020000,
overlapping the running kernel. After enabling GSWIP-R receive, ARP bytes
replaced setup_frame instructions. arch_mem_init() scans reserved-memory
before bootmem_init() reserves the kernel, allowing a dynamic allocation
to claim the kernel range.

Protect GRX500's kernel before the DT allocation pass. The later identical
reservation in bootmem_init() is harmless. Keep other MIPS platforms on
their existing path while this port is under hardware bring-up.

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
@@ -643,6 +643,13 @@ static void __init arch_mem_init(char **cmdline_p)
 
 	check_kernel_sections_mem();
 
+	/* Dynamic CBM pools must never occupy the running GRX500 kernel.
+	 * bootmem_init() reserves this range too late for the DT scan below.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SOC_GRX500))
+		memblock_reserve(__pa_symbol(&_text),
+				__pa_symbol(&_end) - __pa_symbol(&_text));
+
 	early_init_fdt_reserve_self();
 	early_init_fdt_scan_reserved_mem();
 
